# MySQL — Hostinger hPanel > Databases (free, included in the plan).
# For local dev: docker compose up -d  →  mysql://propia:propia@localhost:3306/propia
#
# This is the app's connection and the one an agent is given. In production it
# should be a **read-only** user (SELECT on the schema): that is enough for
# `npm run db:status` and for every `--dry` run of a `cron:*` / `seed:*` job,
# which is all an automated contributor ever needs. `tsx` does not read this
# file — export the value in the shell before running any script.
DATABASE_URL=mysql://user:password@localhost:3306/propia

# The owner (read-write) user, for the runs that actually write —
# `npm run cron:cuotas` without --dry, `seed:*`, `import:csv`, `user:create`,
# `db:migrate`, and `db:status -- --probe`.
#
# **Keep this on your own machine only and never give it to an agent.** The
# split is the whole safety story of the operations layer: an agent holding the
# read-only DATABASE_URL can look at production and preview any job, and cannot
# change a row. A writing CLI run picks DATABASE_URL_RW ?? DATABASE_URL
# (scripts/db-credential.ts), so leaving this empty is fine on a machine that
# has one credential for both jobs — nothing changes from how it worked before.
# The Next.js app itself always uses DATABASE_URL: on Hostinger that env var is
# the read-write user, because the site inserts leads and listings.
DATABASE_URL_RW=

# Outbound messaging — OPTIONAL. Leads are stored in MySQL first and the panel
# reads them from there, so the portal works with none of these set. A webhook
# adds outbound delivery: a WhatsApp OTP at publish, and a copy of each lead
# pushed to whatever CRM you point it at (GoHighLevel, n8n, your own endpoint).
# Without it the publish wizard skips phone verification instead of issuing a
# code nobody can receive.
#
# The same endpoint also receives operator alerts — {"event":"operator_alert"}
# with kind "new_lead" or "review_submitted" — so a flow can forward "go look"
# to WhatsApp while routing {"event":"lead"} into the CRM. With no webhook set
# there is no alert: /admin badges the review queue and the last 24 h of leads,
# which needs no configuration at all.
LEAD_WEBHOOK_URL=
# New-lead and new-listing alerts to the operator's phone via a Telegram bot.
# Alerts only — unlike LEAD_WEBHOOK_URL this does NOT turn on WhatsApp code
# verification in /publicar. Both must be set; unset = no Telegram alerts.
#   1. In Telegram, message @BotFather, send /newbot, copy the token it gives.
#   2. Send any message to your new bot, then open
#      https://api.telegram.org/bot<TOKEN>/getUpdates and copy "chat":{"id": …}.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
# Site-health alerts use the same Telegram chat (and OPERATOR_EMAIL, when email
# sending is configured): a server error (throttled: the same error at most once
# an hour, ten alerts an hour in total), and `check:live` — a minute after every
# deploy and once a day, it loads each live door's home, evergreen pages and a
# sitemap sample and names any URL that is not a 200. No variable needed.
#   LIVE_CHECK=0        — turn the after-deploy check off.
#   LIVE_CHECK_HOSTS    — comma list of hosts to check instead of every live door.
# Partner alerts on Telegram (docs/plan-agency-2026-09-26.md batch 4): a lead
# shared with them, a buyer's email reply to a shared lead, the unanswered-lead
# reminder. Uses the same bot as TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN. All three below + the token
# must be set, or /agencia/perfil shows "not enabled" instead of a link.
#   TELEGRAM_BOT_USERNAME   — the bot's @username from @BotFather, without the @.
#   TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_SECRET — random, 16+ characters, only A-Z a-z 0-9 _ -
#                             (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`). Signs each partner's
#                             "Conectar Telegram" link and authenticates
#                             /api/telegram. Changing it breaks unused links, not
#                             chats already connected. Then register the webhook
#                             once (docs/plan-agency-2026-09-26.md batch 4):
#   curl "https://api.telegram.org/bot<TOKEN>/setWebhook?url=https://inmobiliaria.com.py/api/telegram&secret_token=<TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_SECRET>"
TELEGRAM_BOT_USERNAME=
TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Bearer for POST /api/cron/tick, the hourly scheduler (src/lib/cron-tick.ts:
# partner reminders, analytics rollup, geo + sessions once a day, and up to 15
# listing translations when a translation key below is set). The
# Cloudflare Worker in workers/inbound-email/ calls it; the same value goes into
# that Worker as a secret (its README). 16+ characters; unset = the endpoint
# answers 503 and nothing is scheduled.
CRON_SECRET=
# Email — Cloudflare Email Sending (REST API, src/lib/email.ts). Server-only,
# set in hPanel. Both CLOUDFLARE_* must be set; unset = no email at all, and
# nothing pretends one was sent. Sends: operator alerts (to OPERATOR_EMAIL),
# the FSBO owner's "new enquiry", the seeker's confirmation (when they left an
# address) and "a lead was shared with you" to the partner's login email.
#   CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID  — dashboard → any zone → Overview → Account ID.
#   CLOUDFLARE_EMAIL_TOKEN — an API token with only "Email Sending: Edit".
#   EMAIL_FROM             — optional. Always an address on the verified mail.
#                            subdomain, never the root domain (root is Email
#                            Routing's). Default:
#                            Inmobiliaria Paraguay <avisos@mail.inmobiliaria.com.py>
#   OPERATOR_EMAIL         — optional. Where operator alerts go; unset = no
#                            operator email (Telegram/webhook still work).
# Check it with: npm run email:test -- --to you@example.com --dry, then without --dry.
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
CLOUDFLARE_EMAIL_TOKEN=
EMAIL_FROM=
# Cloudflare Email Sending's daily quota is per ACCOUNT (200 to start, shared by
# every domain, grows with reputation). Set this to the figure the Cloudflare
# dashboard shows once it has been raised. The app counts what THIS server sent
# today (UTC, reset by a restart) and alerts the operator (Telegram +
# OPERATOR_EMAIL) at 80% and 100%; a Cloudflare quota refusal alerts at once.
# The dashboard is the exact meter. Unset or invalid = 200.
EMAIL_DAILY_QUOTA=
OPERATOR_EMAIL=
# Password reset ("¿Olvidaste tu contraseña?" on /login → /recuperar).
# Server-only, set in hPanel, then restart. The reset link is a stateless
# HMAC-SHA256 token signed with this key (src/lib/auth/reset-token.ts): no
# table, valid 60 minutes, and dead the moment the password changes.
#   AUTH_TOKEN_SECRET — at least 32 characters, e.g. `openssl rand -base64 48`.
#                       Unset (or shorter) = no "forgot password" link and
#                       /recuperar says the feature is unavailable. It is ALSO
#                       hidden while the two CLOUDFLARE_* email vars above are
#                       unset: a link that cannot be delivered is not offered.
#                       Changing it invalidates every link already sent.
AUTH_TOKEN_SECRET=
# Inbound email — the inbox (waves E2 + E3; workers/inbound-email/README.md).
# Server-only, set in hPanel.
#   INBOUND_EMAIL_SECRET — the Worker ↔ app shared secret (HMAC-SHA256), the
#                          SAME value as `wrangler secret put INBOUND_EMAIL_SECRET`.
#                          At least 16 characters (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`).
#                          Unset = /api/inbound-email answers 503 (the Worker
#                          then forwards everything to FALLBACK_FORWARD) AND no
#                          lead email carries a lead-…@ Reply-To. Set it only
#                          AFTER the Worker and the Email Routing rules are live,
#                          or buyers' replies go to an address nothing receives.
#   EMAIL_ROOT_SENDING   — `true` only once the ROOT domain (inmobiliaria.com.py)
#                          is onboarded in Cloudflare Email Sending too. Then
#                          /admin/inbox replies go out AS hola@ / anton@;
#                          otherwise from EMAIL_FROM with Reply-To hola@.
#   EMAIL_REPLY_DOMAIN   — optional. Where lead-<id>-<sig>@ addresses live;
#                          default EMAIL_FROM's domain (mail.inmobiliaria.com.py).
#   R2_INBOX_BUCKET      — optional, recommended. A PRIVATE R2 bucket (no public
#                          access) for email attachments, same R2_* keys. Unset =
#                          the photo bucket under random `inbox/` keys, which are
#                          never rendered but are public-read if ever leaked.
INBOUND_EMAIL_SECRET=
EMAIL_ROOT_SENDING=
EMAIL_REPLY_DOMAIN=
R2_INBOX_BUCKET=
# Historical alias for LEAD_WEBHOOK_URL; either name works.
GHL_WEBHOOK_URL=
GHL_API_KEY=

# VenderCRM — a copy of every lead, filed under the door's own CRM site.
# One key per door (per VenderCRM "site"), server-only, set in hPanel and
# never committed. A door whose key is unset keeps its leads local-only (and
# on LEAD_WEBHOOK_URL if that is set); it never borrows another door's key.
# These keys do NOT turn on WhatsApp code verification in /publicar.
# Existing leads: `npm run crm:backfill -- --dry`, then without --dry.
VENDERCRM_BASE_URL=
VENDERCRM_KEY_INMOBILIARIA=
VENDERCRM_KEY_EN=
VENDERCRM_KEY_TERRENO=
VENDERCRM_KEY_LAND=
VENDERCRM_KEY_AGENTS=
VENDERCRM_KEY_RENT=
VENDERCRM_KEY_ALQUILER=
VENDERCRM_KEY_DEVS=

# Cloudflare R2 — listing photos. Free tier: 10 GB, zero egress.
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
R2_BUCKET=propia-images
# Public delivery URL for the bucket. Use the bucket's own public URL
# (https://pub-<hash>.r2.dev) or a custom domain YOU HAVE MAPPED in
# Cloudflare. Do NOT point this at a domain that isn't set up —
# img.propia.com.py was the old placeholder and propia.com.py is not owned,
# so leaving it would 404 every photo the day R2 goes live (audit F64).
# Leave empty until the bucket exists: empty = stored keys pass through
# unchanged, which keeps imported remote-URL photos working.
R2_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=

# Portal contact identity (src/config/contact.ts) — footer, /contacto,
# privacy policy and Organization JSON-LD all read these. Both are OPTIONAL
# and have no fallback: leave them empty and the site shows no address and no
# WhatsApp CTA, routing everyone to the on-site lead form instead. Fill them
# in only with a mailbox/number that is actually monitored (audit F10).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ means Next inlines them at BUILD time — a rebuild is required
# after changing either, not just a restart. Both are per-deployment, not
# per-vertical: the rental doors (alquiler.com.py, rentparaguay.com) read the
# same NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTACT_WHATSAPP as the marketplace doors — there is no
# separate rental WhatsApp number in config (fable/plan-rentparaguay.md §7).
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTACT_EMAIL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTACT_WHATSAPP=

# EUR option on the English marketplace doors (realestateinparaguay.com,
# landforsaleparaguay.com): EUR per 1 USD, e.g. 0.92. OPTIONAL — unset or
# invalid (anything but a plain decimal between 0.5 and 1.5) and there is no
# USD / EUR switch and no euro amount anywhere. Update by hand now and then;
# visitors are shown every EUR figure as an approximation ("≈ €…", rounded).
# Server-side and read at request time (src/lib/eur-rate.ts), NOT
# NEXT_PUBLIC_*: after changing it in hPanel a restart is enough, no rebuild.
USD_EUR_RATE=

# Claude API — barrio guides + EN translations (batch jobs, NEVER the request
# path). `npm run cron:translate` fills listings.title_en/description_en for
# the English door (and the hourly /api/cron/tick runs it, 15 rows a tick, once
# either key is set); with no key it refuses to run rather than writing anything,
# and the site is unaffected — publishing never calls the API, so it cannot be
# blocked by one being down (src/lib/translate.ts explains why there is no
# publish-time hook).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Optional: the model cron:translate uses. Defaults to claude-opus-5.
ANTHROPIC_TRANSLATION_MODEL=

# Translation providers for `cron:translate`: Gemini first, then Claude
# (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY above) — either may be set; a row that fails on one falls
# through to the other. (DeepL was removed 2026-09-26: it translated place
# names — "Sajonia" became "Saxony" — because it never sees the glossary prompt.)
#
# Gemini: the cheap ongoing path —
# $0.30/$2.50 per million input/output tokens on gemini-3.5-flash-lite (the
# default; override with GEMINI_TRANSLATION_MODEL) with no hidden token
# overhead, unlike gemini-3.6-flash — see src/lib/translate.ts's
# GEMINI_MODEL comment. Get one at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_TRANSLATION_MODEL=

# AI reply suggestions — the "Sugerir respuesta" button on reply boxes in
# /admin/inbox, /admin/leads and /agencia/leads (src/lib/ai-reply.ts). It only
# fills the textarea; a person always presses Send. Uses the SAME keys as
# cron:translate above: with neither GEMINI_API_KEY nor ANTHROPIC_API_KEY set
# the button is hidden (never an error). One call per click, 30 s timeout, 30
# clicks per user per hour; token use is logged and /admin/ajustes shows the
# month's estimated cost.
# Which provider drafts: gemini (default, cheapest) | claude. If the chosen one
# has no key and the other does, the other is used.
AI_REPLY_PROVIDER=
# Optional model override for whichever provider runs. Defaults:
# gemini-3.5-flash-lite (Gemini) / claude-sonnet-5-5 (Claude).
AI_REPLY_MODEL=
# Optional kill switch: "true" hides the button while keeping the keys for
# cron:translate.
AI_REPLY_DISABLED=

# Canonical host — the Spanish marketplace primary since the D6 flip
# (2026-09-04). It is not only an origin string: src/config/verticals.ts derives
# DEFAULT from it, so it decides the locale, filters and copy of every request
# that arrives without a known Host header. Never edit this and the vertical
# entries separately — they must agree, or an unknown-host request gets one
# door's locale while the known hosts get another's.
#
# Only a host that is a key in src/config/verticals.ts may go here. Several
# domains this project used earlier are not owned by the founder, and pointing
# canonicals at one of those breaks them sitewide.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ means Next inlines it at BUILD time: changing it on Hostinger
# needs a rebuild, not a restart, which is why this one item cannot ship in a
# commit (CLAUDE.md backlog 2).
NEXT_PUBLIC_CANONICAL_HOST=inmobiliaria.com.py

# Google Search Console report in /admin/google (src/lib/search-console.ts).
# A service-account key (the whole JSON, or it base64-encoded) whose
# client_email is added as a user on each Search Console property. Unset =
# the page shows the setup steps. Properties default to sc-domain:<host> for
# every live door; GSC_PROPERTIES (comma list) overrides.
GSC_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=
GSC_PROPERTIES=

# WhatsApp Cloud API (Meta) — the founder's business number in /admin/inbox and
# under leads (src/lib/whatsapp.ts, docs/log/whatsapp-inbox.md has the full
# Meta setup). All four of ACCESS_TOKEN, PHONE_NUMBER_ID, APP_SECRET and
# VERIFY_TOKEN set = on; anything less = off (panels hidden, /api/whatsapp 503).
# Webhook URL to give Meta: https://inmobiliaria.com.py/api/whatsapp
# Permanent system-user token (whatsapp_business_messaging +
# whatsapp_business_management). Secret: never in a file, hPanel only.
WHATSAPP_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# "Phone number ID" from the app's WhatsApp → API Setup page (digits).
WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=
# "WhatsApp Business Account ID" from the same page. Informational.
WHATSAPP_WABA_ID=
# App settings → Basic → App secret. Signs every webhook (X-Hub-Signature-256).
WHATSAPP_APP_SECRET=
# Any long random string you choose (openssl rand -hex 24); typed into Meta's
# webhook form as the "Verify token".
WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN=
# Optional Graph API version, e.g. v23.0 (the default). Set it to the version
# Meta's dashboard shows when this one is retired.
WHATSAPP_GRAPH_VERSION=
